========================================================================
MECHANISM (why eprintln sees it and stmt println does not)
========================================================================

Stmt rail (`c_emit_print.oo` L19–30):

```
while sp < n {
    sk = token
    if COMMA || RPAREN || SEMI { break }   # no depth
    if IDENT && __sec__sn == "1" { refuse }
    sp++
}
# then c_emit_expr_c — emit only; no second refuse
```

`println(("x") + tok)` tokens after LPAREN:
`LPAREN STRING RPAREN PLUS IDENT(tok) RPAREN`

Scan hits the **grouping** `RPAREN` and stops. Never looks at `tok`.
`c_emit_expr_c` then lowers the full `(("x") + tok)` and prints it.

HEAD / ELF check rail (`c_emit_secret.oo` as compiled into 07:49):

```
optional skip LPAREN
while tokens:
    if RPAREN { stop }          # no depth
    if IDENT { refuse_resolved }
```

Same first-`)` stop. Live `check` rc=0 `OK` on the hole shapes.

WT check rail (12:28, **not in this ELF**):

```
depth = 1
LPAREN → depth++
RPAREN → depth--; stop only if depth <= 0
IDENT  → refuse_resolved
```

That would close **check** (and therefore emit-c front-door) for both
names **after a rebuild**. It does **not** change the stmt scan. This
peer did not rebuild. Live ELF still first-`)`.

Free-call rail (`c_emit_lower.oo` L90 + guard L213–226):

```
args = joined C text   # e.g. oo_str_concat((oo_str_lit("x")), tok)
c_secret_emit_guard(..., "eprintln", ..., args)
c_guard_scan_idents  # string-aware; still slices bare ident tok
```

That is the only rail that still sees `tok` after a nested `)` on
this host.

`println((1), tok)` is **not** this miss: after `c_emit_expr_c`
consumes `(1)`, the **next** arg scan sees `tok`. Check still FN both
on the ELF. That is the harness wave-2 rail, not this REJECT.

